{"id": "EUVD-2026-81947", "enisaUuid": "a5e6b1ac-c4e0-3953-b7fc-47b622832c7f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxsk: honor XDP_TX_METADATA in zero-copy path\n\nThe zero-copy path reads TX metadata whenever the UMEM has metadata space,\neven if the descriptor does not set XDP_TX_METADATA. Pass descriptor\noptions through the metadata helpers and ignore metadata unless the option\nis set.\n\nThis does not fix the existing per-WQE metadata handling for mlx5 MPWQEs.\nOnly the descriptor that starts a session passes through\nxsk_tx_metadata_request() and configures offload state shared by the batch.\nMetadata on descriptors joining an open session is therefore not validated\nand does not configure its requested offloads. In addition, a non-NULL\nmetadata pointer from such a descriptor is treated as a timestamp\ncompletion request even when XDP_TXMD_FLAGS_TIMESTAMP is not set, so its\nmetadata union can be overwritten with an unrequested timestamp. Fixing\nmixed metadata states within one MPWQE requires a separate change.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:49:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ba0d143e471c85f8a116707c0b42bf046b0a7b3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/53a5b262d706b572840cbe8feae392538077ee19", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf9387488d6394845076928c6ca5315ce5d84f54", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a6e4b9a6deb9362ef7a0706c70d674e92fe1411a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5vhq-jqrp-ph25", "CVE-2026-90086"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1631f6bf-735f-3b62-ab36-a97c21d4296a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "48eb03dd26304c24f03bdbb9382e89c8564e71df <8ba0d143e471c85f8a116707c0b42bf046b0a7b3"}, {"id": "1919c9bc-31a8-3fe4-85dd-16b873b5f8f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "19dc1182-577f-37eb-9985-b6755c8ed713", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "48eb03dd26304c24f03bdbb9382e89c8564e71df <53a5b262d706b572840cbe8feae392538077ee19"}, {"id": "21a9b139-4ec7-3a36-bd68-206a8dab5034", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "4e0ecf45-a6b9-3921-a2e6-37523451d1cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "60fe35c5-5ca5-3d72-be39-5e50fc3a569c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "48eb03dd26304c24f03bdbb9382e89c8564e71df <bf9387488d6394845076928c6ca5315ce5d84f54"}, {"id": "79e22b5a-32c5-3e3c-8b2e-2b829ba29999", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "89d7276d-a89f-355f-9dc6-3e61a10188f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "92f4fc37-bdb6-3fe2-a294-d9d6d35eaefc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "48eb03dd26304c24f03bdbb9382e89c8564e71df <a6e4b9a6deb9362ef7a0706c70d674e92fe1411a"}, {"id": "b57289d5-40c0-31ba-b760-fa4e8f191332", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d9e7a92b-a829-305b-81b8-13f9c543ecc1", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}